    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d938">

                <pb facs="0845" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/418: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-27T20:00:00-05:00">December 27, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>379. Department’s 377, December 26, 6 p.m.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d938-f1"/> The
                    Department has telegraphed Shanghai as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Allison and staff should proceed on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Oahu</hi> as scheduled but not attempt to land at Nanking until
                            after the first of January.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Allison and staff are returning to Nanking to reoccupy the American Embassy
                    property, to protect and be of assistance to American nationals and their
                    interests and to handle other official business.</p>
                <pb facs="0846" n="839" xml:id="pg839"/>
                <p>Please call at the Foreign Office and, referring to the request of the Japanese
                    authorities at Shanghai that our officers postpone their departure until after
                    the first of January, state that Allison and staff are proceeding as scheduled
                    on the <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> which is leaving Shanghai on the 28th
                    and request that instructions be issued to the appropriate Japanese authorities
                    to the end that, when Allison and staff arrive at Nanking there may be no
                    interference in connection with their landing or functioning at Nanking.<anchor
                        n="57" xml:id="d938-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d938-f1" n="56" xml:id="d938-f1-content">
